                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "There are many problems I encountered with this game, but the purpose of the developers putting it in Early Access is to fix issues and to make improvements.\n\nFirst here's what I like:\n\n-Good graphics\n-Great, fluent animation\n-If this game persists, then I'm sure it will be a fantastic single-player experience to enjoy in your freetime.\n\nHere's are the problems in it's current state (which can be fixed, of course):\n\n-There is little to nothing to do, it seems like a sandbox\n\n-When attacking certain animals, such as the rabbit, there is a very small hitbox, I would suggest testing and altering hitboxes for certain AI.\n\n-Combinations of certain animations are buggy. When I pressed e to eat a fish after catching it, it permanantly changed my e command to the fish eating animation - instead of howling. This is fixed after making a new save.\n\n-*** The AI seems to be the biggest issue. Especially the hunters' AI. When playing sometimes I heard a glitched gunshot sound from a hunter when there were no hunters nearby. \n     -Additionally, there are far too many hunters spawning in the map.  \n     -The hunters should not have such distinct and one-way coding. For example, every hunter and even the same hunter has the same attack radius ( I noticed a hunter chasing a deer and everytime he would catch up to shoot the deer he would go back to running because the deer kept repeatedly going out of his range after catching up. So you should make the hunter have the chance to shoot at greater distances with a lesser chance of hitting the target). I think there should be a probability of the hunter shooting at certain ranges at certain time intervals. \n\n     -The AI don't seem to realize that there is an object between the two people. So they will continue to shoot even if there is a tree in the way. And if an object is blocking the AI's sight, they will still detect you.\n   \n\nFinally, for a game like this I would rather have you focus with environmental struggles other than the hunters. Encountering hunters should be much more rare and harsh experience. \n\n\n\n     \n",
